  "result_text": "**Enterprise revenue for 2026 Q2 (April 1 \u2013 June 30) was $925,797.78.** That comes from 199 orders.\n\nFor comparison, the other segments in Q2 were Mid-Market at $542,840.57 and SMB at $223,120.39.\n\n**A plain join would have overstated Enterprise revenue.** `accounts.csv` has 70 rows but only 60 distinct accounts, because 10 accounts appear more than once. The extra rows are region or owner changes, each with a new `valid_from` date. Joining orders straight onto that file duplicates those accounts' orders and gives about $1,227,245, roughly $301K too high.\n\n**Segment never changes for any account.** Every account has the same segment on all of its rows, so I mapped each account to one segment and then summed. Segment doesn't depend on the `valid_from` date. If you wanted revenue by region or owner as of the order date, the versioned rows would matter, but that wasn't the question.\n\n**The order data looked clean.** There are 2,077 orders with unique IDs and no missing or non-positive amounts. Every order's account exists in the accounts file. Dates run from 2026-01-01 to 2026-06-30, so Q2 is fully covered.\n\nI saved the output in `/var/folders/4_/s6fbcjyn4b13xdxkd3lv0kw00000gn/T/arm-s22c-baseline-4dd89a5s/work/result.txt`."
